# Everything here is either recreated inside the image or irrelevant to it.
#
# Excluding it matters for two reasons. The obvious one is that the whole
# context is tarred and sent to the daemon on every build. The bigger one is
# cache stability: docker/clam.Dockerfile does `COPY . /clam`, and that layer's
# hash covers every file in the context, so a host-side `ninja` run that touches
# build-release/ invalidates the COPY and with it every layer below -- including
# the expensive crab, ldd and apron steps.

# Host build trees. clam.Dockerfile deletes /clam/build, /clam/debug and
# /clam/release immediately after the COPY, and these change constantly.
build
build-*
install-*
debug
release

# Third-party sources. clam.Dockerfile removes these too; the crab and extra
# targets re-clone them inside the image.
crab
sea-dsa
llvm-seahorn

# Nothing in the build reads clam's own history: find_package(Git) in
# CMakeLists.txt only locates the git executable, to clone the dependencies
# above.
.git
.github

**/__pycache__
*.pyc

.DS_Store
